================================================================================
ITU resources this work extends
================================================================================

ITU AI Readiness reference implementation (MIT License)
  https://github.com/CrashingGuru/ITUAIReadiness
  The file simulation/data/framework/dimensions.json is redistributed here at
  data/sources/INTL/02_ITU_AI_Readiness_dimensions.json. Our AI Readiness map is
  GENERATED from it at build time (scripts/gen_ai_readiness_map.py) so that no ITU
  label is ever retyped by us.

ITU Sandbox training dataset
  https://github.com/CrashingGuru/Sandbox_Training
  Used to locate the official eGazette URLs for the Telecommunications Act 2023 and
  the Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023. Clause text in this repository is
  extracted by us from the official eGazette PDFs, not copied from that dataset.

ITU-T Recommendations referenced (not redistributed)
  Y.3172  Architectural framework for machine learning in future networks
  Y.3173  Framework for evaluating intelligence level of future networks
  Y.3181  Architectural framework for ML sandbox
  X.1303  Common Alerting Protocol (CAP 1.2)
  E.106   International Emergency Preference Scheme
  Q.3057 / Q.3062 / Q.3063  Signature-based calling party authentication
  ITU-D Guidelines for National Emergency Telecommunication Plans (2020)

This project is ALIGNED WITH and MAPPED TO the above. It is not certified by,
approved by, or endorsed by the ITU, and no such claim is made anywhere in it.

================================================================================
Primary source documents
================================================================================

Source PDFs are NOT redistributed in this repository. Each is recorded in
data/sources/MANIFEST.yaml with its official URL, SHA-256 and verification
status, and is re-fetched by scripts/fetch_sources.py. This avoids redistributing
third-party documents whose licence terms we have not cleared.

Clause TEXT extracted from the following is included as clause records with
attribution, page number and hash:

  Government of India, eGazette (public domain in India under s.52(1)(q) of the
  Copyright Act 1957, which exempts reproduction of any Act, rule or order):
    The Telecommunications Act, 2023 (Act 44 of 2023)
      https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2023/250880.pdf
    The Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (Act 22 of 2023)
      https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2023/248045.pdf
    Telecommunications (Temporary Suspension of Services) Rules, 2024,
      G.S.R. 724(E), 22 Nov 2024

  United States Government (works of the US Government are not subject to
  copyright under 17 U.S.C. s.105):
    47 CFR 4.17, Federal Register Vol. 87 No. 189, 30 Sep 2022

Documents fetched for verification but whose text is NOT redistributed here, as
their licence terms have not been cleared:
    CERT-In Directions, 28 Apr 2022 (cert-in.org.in)
    SOP for Telecommunication Services During Disasters (DITT, Bhutan)
    Standing Orders on Disaster 2019 (MoDMR, Bangladesh; ADRC mirror)

================================================================================
Scenario calibration
================================================================================

Cyclone Amphan timings are taken from the IMD RSMC New Delhi press release.
Network impact figures are reported aggregates (COAI via Deccan Herald; BTRC via
Dhaka Tribune for Remal 2024). Per-cell network state is SIMULATED and is labelled
as such everywhere it appears. See docs/limits.md.
